  "result": "I've re-planned NRS-484B-270-2b, and the validator accepts all three nodes: `NRS_484B_270_2b_o1`, `_o2` and `_o3`.\n\n**Why it came back:** the three nodes compose `NRS_484B_217_2`, which a repair session revised in iteration 5. Their link pointed at the old version (the `pin_mismatch`). The current version is accepted and usable for building, and it is still the rule the text names (\"Except as otherwise provided in … 484B.217\"). The re-plan keeps that composition, now against the current record.\n\n**What's unchanged:** nothing else in the returned reason concerned these nodes, and no failing case or label mismatch was reported. So each node keeps the segmentation, mappings, judgement-standard readings and scenarios that the validator accepted in iteration 4. Only one thing was removed: the parameter proposals, because every parameter they named is now in the catalogue.\n\nThe three nodes, in brief:\n- **`_o1` (due care):** a surrogate rule. It judges the pass by its outcome: no contact with the rider, and the rider never has to brake hard while the two are side by side.\n- **`_o2` (pass on the left at a safe distance):** applies only where the rider's lane has one lane in its direction. While side by side, the rider must be on the car's right, with a gap of at least 3 ft or the reading's safe-gap clearance, whichever is larger.\n- **`_o3` (don't move back right until safely clear):** the car must not turn back right until the rider is behind it at a following-headway gap for the road surface.\n\nThere is nothing new for the operator.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/fsw/portfolios/av/projects/av_alpamayo_reasoning/users/wcong/WorldModelSpec/.worktrees/full221-v2/pipeline/traffic-spec-agent/results/full221-1116-1018/iter-006/plan/`:\n- `blueprint.jsonl`\n- `PLAN.md`\n- `aggregates.jsonl` (empty; the law defines no aggregates of its own)",
